**The CSP has no `unsafe-inline` in `style-src`.** A `style="..."` attribute in
served markup is dropped without an error — four progress bars once rendered at
100% because of it. Use a class, or a `data-` attribute with a matching CSS
rule. Setting `element.style` from JavaScript is fine; CSP governs markup, not
CSSOM. Do not weaken the header in `server.js` to make something work.

**Colours come from `tokens.css` only.** Two traps:

- The dark palette is written twice (a media query and an attribute selector
  cannot share a rule). Change one, change both — a test compares them.
- `--ez-accent-ink` is *what sits on the accent fill*; `--ez-accent-text` is
  *the accent used as text on a neutral ground*. Opposites. Same for
  `--ez-crit` / `--ez-crit-ink`.

**Verify contrast, don't estimate it** — measured against the composited
background, in both themes, at desktop and 390px. Let a theme change settle
before measuring or you catch a half-applied frame and get failures that aren't
real.

**Nothing invented.** No testimonials, no user counts, no competitor claims.
Prices are fetched from `/api/plans`, never typed into markup.

`admin.*` here is the only copy of the Control Room — it is deliberately not in
the extension package.
